# Fork locked Robert repos (hard rule)

Operator directive (Phil, 2026-08-14), verbatim intent:

> **Hard Rule: Please copy roberts repos as required when they are
> read-only/locked and rename them so that we can make extensive changes to
> them and check them in to github. Robert will try to merge in my changes
> after I am done. If you have another way that will not block advancing the
> locked code base you can use it. We must be able to copy our changes to the
> github repo and they cannot be local only.**

Context that motivated this: AIC Server needed `create_with_candidates` /
`pim-disc` but could not link it (FIPS `ring`) and could not wait on Robert
to land a `probe` CLI. Agents invented `NETWORK_CREDENTIAL_PROBE_CLI` and
left mix-server `probe` as **uncommitted local** work — that violates
“cannot be local only.”

## The rule

> **When a Robert / mix-server / massman / pim-disc (or sibling) repository
> is read-only or locked for AIC — we cannot push, cannot merge on his
> schedule, or advancing requires extensive changes he has not taken —
> agents MUST NOT leave the work as uncommitted local edits or as a
> process-boundary BLOCKED on a CLI he has not shipped. They MUST either
> (1) copy/fork under an AIC-owned GitHub name, push to GitHub, and pin
> consumers at that git URL + rev, or (2) use an agreed published
> extraction / thin AIC adapter that is already on GitHub and unblocks
> this slice. Local-only clones, gitignored CLIs, and unset
> `NETWORK_CREDENTIAL_PROBE_CLI`-style env gates are forbidden.**

[`reuse-robert-core-first.mdc`](reuse-robert-core-first.mdc) still applies
when upstream is unlocked and reusable. **This rule wins when upstream is
locked or blocked.**

## Preferred path — AIC-owned fork on GitHub

When changes are extensive or Robert cannot take them on AIC’s schedule:

1. **Copy / fork** the locked repo into a **new** AIC-owned GitHub
   repository. Do **not** overwrite `analoginfo-pim/mix-server` or his
   remotes.
2. **Rename** per convention below (`pim-<crate>-aic` or
   `<upstream-name>-aic`).
3. **Push** the working branch: `git push -u origin <branch>`. The source
   of truth for the changed crate **must** be a pushed GitHub repo.
4. **Pin consumers** (`pim-offline-server`, etc.) at that **git URL +
   rev**. A Cargo overlay / `.cargo/config.toml` path patch to a local
   clone is OK for build speed, but the changed crate’s authoritative
   remote must be the AIC GitHub repo.
5. **Record provenance** in the fork README and Cargo metadata: upstream
   remote URL, upstream commit (or tag) forked from, and that Robert may
   merge AIC changes back later.
6. Robert merges from the AIC fork when ready — do not claim the fork
   **is** upstream.

## Allowed alternative that does not block

Use only if it **already** exists on GitHub and unblocks the feature in
**this slice**:

- An agreed published crate / extraction Robert (or AIC) already owns, or
- A thin AIC adapter that does **not** fork business rules (per
  [`reuse-robert-core-first.mdc`](reuse-robert-core-first.mdc)).

**Not** an acceptable alternative:

- A gitignored local-only `pim-disc-cli` (or similar) path
- An unset / invented `NETWORK_CREDENTIAL_PROBE_CLI` (or any product env
  gate) waiting on a CLI Robert has not shipped
- “BLOCKED until Robert lands X” when a fork would advance AIC now

## Rename convention

| Pattern | Example |
| --- | --- |
| `pim-<crate>-aic` | `pim-disc-aic` |
| `<upstream-name>-aic` | `mix-server-aic` |

Host under `https://github.com/analoginfo-pim/` (or the org Phil already
uses for AIC-owned repos). Never push AIC extensive-change branches as if
they were Robert’s canonical `main`.

## Must push — no local-only copies

| State | Verdict |
| --- | --- |
| Changes only under `c:\analog-pim\mix-server` (or any Robert clone), **uncommitted** | **FAIL** |
| Committed locally but **never** `git push -u origin <branch>` to an AIC-owned remote | **FAIL** |
| Pushed to AIC-owned GitHub; consumers pinned to that URL + rev | **PASS** |

`git push -u origin <branch>` is required. Workspace convenience clones
are not the durable store.

## FIPS / `ring` boundary

- Do **not** leave FIPS `ring` linked into `pim-offline-server` to
  “just call” disc APIs in-process.
- The fork may keep disc’s upstream deps. The server still consumes via
  a **process boundary** (out-of-process CLI / service) **or** a
  **ring-free extraction** — document which in the pin / README.
- Honesty on crypto posture remains under
  [`enterprise-compliance.mdc`](enterprise-compliance.mdc) §4.

## Forbidden constructs

- Force-pushing Robert’s remotes or rewriting his `main` on the original
  repo.
- Claiming an AIC fork **is** upstream or renaming over his GitHub repo.
- Leaving extensive changes as uncommitted or unpushed local work under
  a Robert clone.
- Inventing a process-boundary BLOCKED on a CLI / feature he has not
  shipped instead of forking or using an already-published path.
- Gitignored local-only probe CLIs or product configuration that only
  works when an unpublished binary sits on the lab disk.
- Linking `ring` into `pim-offline-server` to bypass the FIPS floor.

## Required agent behavior

1. When reuse is blocked by read-only / locked upstream or schedule:
   prefer an AIC-owned GitHub fork (rename + push + pin), or an already-
   published alternative that unblocks this slice.
2. Record upstream remote + fork-from commit in README and Cargo
   metadata on the AIC repo.
3. Pin consumers to the AIC git URL + rev; path patches are build aids
   only.
4. Document process-boundary vs ring-free extraction for server
   consumption.
5. Commit and push the AIC fork per
   [`auto-commit-push.mdc`](auto-commit-push.mdc); mirror this rule to
   `core-assets/.cursor/rules/` in the same change set (workspace
   `.cursor` is not a git root).
6. Do not stop at “read-only → invent BLOCKED CLI.”

## Worked violation → fix

**Violation.** AIC Server needs `create_with_candidates` from `pim-disc`.
In-process link pulls `ring` (FIPS fail). Agent adds
`NETWORK_CREDENTIAL_PROBE_CLI`, builds a `probe` binary only under the
local `mix-server` tree, never commits or pushes. Slice reports BLOCKED
on “Robert’s probe CLI.”

**Fix.** Fork to `analoginfo-pim/pim-disc-aic` (or `mix-server-aic` as
needed), land the probe (or ring-free extraction) there, `git push -u
origin <branch>`, pin `pim-offline-server` (or the out-of-process
invoker) at that GitHub URL + rev, document process-boundary vs
extraction. Robert merges from the AIC fork later. No local-only probe;
no unset env CLI gate as the delivery path.

